There is a Pathfinder 1e adventure in progress.

The player just declared an intention and we need you to decide what roll they need, if any.

=== PLAYER INTENT ===
<%= @roll_request_context.intent %>

<%= PromptRenderer.render_partial("partials/cast_roster", cast_roster: @roll_request_context.cast_roster) %>

<%= PromptRenderer.render_partial("partials/scene_retrieval", scene_retrieval: @roll_request_context.scene_retrieval) %>

You need to make sequential decisions for this.
- Is it an attack roll? If so, that is all you need to tell us, no other decisions are needed.

<% if @roll_request_context.relevant_rules.any? -%>
- Is it a skill check or saving roll? If so, you need to take the rules below into account.

  <% @roll_request_context.relevant_rules.each_with_index do |rule, idx| -%>
    <%= idx + 1 %>. **<%= rule[:name] %>** (slug: `<%= rule[:slug] %>`)
    <%= rule[:body].to_s.strip.gsub("\n", "\n   ") %>
  <% end -%>
<% else -%>
- Is it a skill check or saving roll? Pick the appropriate rule from your Pathfinder 1e knowledge.
<% end -%>

These fields must come from the chosen rule:
  - `skill`: the name
  - `dc`: the DC appropriate for the player intent.

=== OTHER FIELDS ===
- `target_actor_sheet_id`: when the action will interact directly with a
  creature in CAST ROSTER, copy that entry's `id` (an integer).
- `transition`: "combat_started" only when the action should initiate combat (e.g. player takes an hostile action in a tense room).
- Emit `dc` only for environmental/static checks (climb a wall, jump a chasm) not for opposed rolls.
- `ability_use_claimed`: a spell/feat/item the player declared intention to use explicitly.
- `situational_modifiers`: each entry is `{ "source": "<short phrase>", "modifier": <integer> }`.
  Take the overall context into account in order to adjudicate bonus or penalties.
  

Respond ONLY with valid JSON in this exact FLAT shape (no wrapper keys):
{
  "needs_roll": true,
  "no_roll_reason": null,
  "roll": {
    "type": "skill_check" OR "attack_roll",
    "skill": "Swim",
    "save": null,
    "dc": 10,
    "description": "Short player-facing description.",
    "take_10_eligible": true,
    "take_20_eligible": false,
    "situational_modifiers": [{ "source": "rough water", "modifier": -2 }],
  },
  "transition": null,
  "target_actor_sheet_id": 273,
  "consequences": [],
  "ability_use_claimed": null,
  "mechanical_summary": "One-sentence factual summary.",
  "reasoning": "One short sentence explaining the call.",
  "confidence": "0-100 of how confident you are in the roll request"
}

`consequences` are rare — leave the array empty unless the action has
an automatic non-roll side-effect the player needs to see. When
present, each entry is `{ "description": "<text>" }`.
